      "start": 0,
      "end": 59,
      "text": "The paper reports a random 80/10/10 split of the molecules.",
      "text_sha256": "69233c395f723472130cc6f3d3e9372cf9e0ee3540d4c22edafdc30578d3a560",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-001&noteId=rev-gnn-001-a",
      "source_sha256": "30481b833a1e331a6554ed2794186bfba3ecf7016b70678d8d491e1d99e08326"
    },
    {
      "excerpt_id": "ex_110f92f3599151f1",
      "source_kind": "review",
      "source_id": "rev-gnn-001-a",
      "start": 60,
      "end": 182,
      "text": "Random splits are known to leak near-duplicate scaffolds between train and test, so the reported MAE is likely optimistic.",
      "text_sha256": "4aea7ef6bff915efa676fbe4652683a4df59abcb9199c8c97931438b8add115d",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-001&noteId=rev-gnn-001-a",
      "source_sha256": "30481b833a1e331a6554ed2794186bfba3ecf7016b70678d8d491e1d99e08326"
    },
    {
      "excerpt_id": "ex_845f5eb5621099f5",
      "source_kind": "review",
      "source_id": "rev-gnn-002-a",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 67,
      "text": "The pretraining corpus overlaps with the downstream test molecules.",
      "text_sha256": "7217f5f5452140e190ca9dc38c9aac1985075b2ba43c857d2affed4e77ee0991",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-002&noteId=rev-gnn-002-a",
      "source_sha256": "523ccc30305f67955b24a23f860c5e3699137cf12aff88416b5a6c1511bec9bb"
    },
    {
      "excerpt_id": "ex_ca5fa760fdb45841",
      "source_kind": "decision",
      "source_id": "dec-gnn-001",
      "start": 25,
      "end": 71,
      "text": "the random split likely overstates performance",
      "text_sha256": "b1188787a3179b6328c37c24b4e2f13b5d7e64a2ef17b85d7c12321c419aa734",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-001&noteId=dec-gnn-001",
      "source_sha256": "8d50f325e4ad8e39417cc04147d3ee27c45d8fd1be7c97d5ecd98aaf6807c80a"
    },
    {
      "excerpt_id": "ex_fc88c26e0b31af5e",
      "source_kind": "review",
      "source_id": "rev-gnn-001-b",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 65,
      "text": "All numbers come from a single training run with one random seed.",
      "text_sha256": "0d7b5472269009086dc50a604e98a22d476ff659b5eed7cd74c744ac15299f00",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-001&noteId=rev-gnn-001-b",
      "source_sha256": "d36b1f9452c00bdcf6ee593f13c589c6602bfd52d498b2adce2db97c7bf25bdd"
    },
    {
      "excerpt_id": "ex_4b76d98627bb3f0c",
      "source_kind": "review",
      "source_id": "rev-gnn-001-b",
      "start": 66,
      "end": 158,
      "text": "Without error bars across seeds it is impossible to tell whether the 3% improvement is real.",
      "text_sha256": "9ad7066b7817f78221ab28aa4be425a7fc2ace2db305bfec0c30b2d61f68ac10",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-001&noteId=rev-gnn-001-b",
      "source_sha256": "d36b1f9452c00bdcf6ee593f13c589c6602bfd52d498b2adce2db97c7bf25bdd"
    },
    {
      "excerpt_id": "ex_6ec54fbcbb2ccae1",
      "source_kind": "review",
      "source_id": "rev-gnn-003-b",
      "start": 267,
      "end": 313,
      "text": "A single seed is used for every ensemble size.",
      "text_sha256": "8c8cbb924781e2a79cfcf6d8c43899ec1d56d3ccaf62d5818df4d5747dd4ab54",
      "source_url": "https://example.org/fake-venue/forum?id=gnn-003&noteId=rev-gnn-003-b",
